  "term": "crying-cat syndrome",
  "definition": "Crying-cat syndrome is a genetic condition seen in infancy that results from deletion of the short arm of chromosome 5. It is associated with a cry resembling that of a cat, poor growth, very small head size, intellectual disability, spastic weakness in all four limbs, and characteristic facial and genital differences.",
